„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter2¨sections›…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkThe word that the LORD spake against Babylon and against the land of the Chaldeans by Jeremiah the prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŞDeclare ye among the nations, and publish, and set up a standard; publish, and conceal not: say, Babylon is taken, Bel is confounded, Merodach is broken in pieces; her idols are confounded, her images are broken in pieces.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶For out of the north there cometh up a nation against her, which shall make her land desolate, and none shall dwell therein: they shall remove, they shall depart, both man and beast.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»In those days, and in that time, saith the LORD, the children of Israel shall come, they and the children of Judah together, going and weeping: they shall go, and seek the LORD their God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥They shall ask the way to Zion with their faces thitherward, saying, Come, and let us join ourselves to the LORD in a perpetual covenant that shall not be forgotten.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉMy people hath been lost sheep: their shepherds have caused them to go astray, they have turned them away on the mountains: they have gone from mountain to hill, they have forgotten their restingplace.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAll that found them have devoured them: and their adversaries said, We offend not, because they have sinned against the LORD, the habitation of justice, even the LORD, the hope of their fathers.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse
¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Remove out of the midst of Babylon, and go forth out of the land of the Chaldeans, and be as the he goats before the flocks.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚFor, lo, I will raise and cause to come up against Babylon an assembly of great nations from the north country: and they shall set themselves in array against her; from thence she shall be taken: their arrows shall be as of a mighty expert man; none shall return in vain.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd Chaldea shall be a spoil: all that spoil her shall be satisfied, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse
…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’Because ye were glad, because ye rejoiced, O ye destroyers of mine heritage, because ye are grown fat as the heifer at grass, and bellow as bulls;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ your mother shall be sore confounded; she that bare you shall be ashamed: behold, the hindermost of the nations shall be a wilderness, a dry land, and a desert.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®Because of the wrath of the LORD it shall not be inhabited, but it shall be wholly desolate: every one that goeth by Babylon shall be astonished, and hiss at all her plagues.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Put yourselves in array against Babylon round about: all ye that bend the bow, shoot at her, spare no arrows: for she hath sinned against the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËShout against her round about: she hath given her hand: her foundations are fallen, her walls are thrown down: for it is the vengeance of the LORD: take vengeance upon her; as she hath done, do unto her.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑCut off the sower from Babylon, and him that handleth the sickle in the time of harvest: for fear of the oppressing sword they shall turn every one to his people, and they shall flee every one to his own land.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Israel is a scattered sheep; the lions have driven him away: first the king of Assyria hath devoured him; and last this Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon hath broken his bones.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšTherefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will punish the king of Babylon and his land, as I have punished the king of Assyria.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And I will bring Israel again to his habitation, and he shall feed on Carmel and Bashan, and his soul shall be satisfied upon mount Ephraim and Gilead.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞIn those days, and in that time, saith the LORD, the iniquity of Israel shall be sought for, and there shall be none; and the sins of Judah, and they shall not be found: for I will pardon them whom I reserve.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÅGo up against the land of Merathaim, even against it, and against the inhabitants of Pekod: waste and utterly destroy after them, saith the LORD, and do according to all that I have commanded thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;A sound of battle is in the land, and of great destruction.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrHow is the hammer of the whole earth cut asunder and broken! how is Babylon become a desolation among the nations!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§I have laid a snare for thee, and thou art also taken, O Babylon, and thou wast not aware: thou art found, and also caught, because thou hast striven against the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤The LORD hath opened his armoury, and hath brought forth the weapons of his indignation: for this is the work of the Lord GOD of hosts in the land of the Chaldeans.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰Come against her from the utmost border, open her storehouses: cast her up as heaps, and destroy her utterly: let nothing of her be left.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}Slay all her bullocks; let them go down to the slaughter: woe unto them! for their day is come, the time of their visitation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•The voice of them that flee and escape out of the land of Babylon, to declare in Zion the vengeance of the LORD our God, the vengeance of his temple.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter2«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚCall together the archers against Babylon: all ye that bend the bow, camp against it round about; let none thereof escape: recompense her according to her work; according to all that she hath done, do unto her: for she hath been proud against the LORD, against the Holy One of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwTherefore shall her young men fall in the streets, and all her men of war shall be cut off in that day, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Behold, I am against thee, O thou most proud, saith the Lord GOD of hosts: for thy day is come, the time that I will visit thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜And the most proud shall stumble and fall, and none shall raise him up: and I will kindle a fire in his cities, and it shall devour all round about him.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter2«first_verse!ªlast_verse"¦verses’„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The children of Israel and the children of Judah were oppressed together: and all that took them captives held them fast; they refused to let them go.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªTheir Redeemer is strong; The LORD of hosts is his name: he shall throughly plead their cause, that he may give rest to the land, and disquiet the inhabitants of Babylon.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book§chapter2«first_verse#ªlast_verse(¦verses–„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€A sword is upon the Chaldeans, saith the LORD, and upon the inhabitants of Babylon, and upon her princes, and upon her wise men.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkA sword is upon the liars; and they shall dote: a sword is upon her mighty men; and they shall be dismayed.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍA sword is upon their horses, and upon their chariots, and upon all the mingled people that are in the midst of her; and they shall become as women: a sword is upon her treasures; and they shall be robbed.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙA drought is upon her waters; and they shall be dried up: for it is the land of graven images, and they are mad upon their idols.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙèTherefore the wild beasts of the desert with the wild beasts of the islands shall dwell there, and the owls shall dwell therein: and it shall be no more inhabited for ever; neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAs God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah and the neighbour cities thereof, saith the LORD; so shall no man abide there, neither shall any son of man dwell therein.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book§chapter2«first_verse)ªlast_verse+¦verses“„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBehold, a people shall come from the north, and a great nation, and many kings shall be raised up from the coasts of the earth.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìThey shall hold the bow and the lance: they are cruel, and will not shew mercy: their voice shall roar like the sea, and they shall ride upon horses, every one put in array, like a man to the battle, against thee, O daughter of Babylon.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒThe king of Babylon hath heard the report of them, and his hands waxed feeble: anguish took hold of him, and pangs as of a woman in travail.¦layout ªlast_verse+…¤book§chapter2«first_verse,ªlast_verse.¦verses“„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ4Behold, he shall come up like a lion from the swelling of Jordan unto the habitation of the strong: but I will make them suddenly run away from her: and who is a chosen man, that I may appoint over her? for who is like me? and who will appoint me the time? and who is that shepherd that will stand before me?¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚTherefore hear ye the counsel of the LORD, that he hath taken against Babylon; and his purposes, that he hath purposed against the land of the Chaldeans: Surely the least of the flock shall draw them out: surely he shall make their habitation desolate with them.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAt the noise of the taking of Babylon the earth is moved, and the cry is heard among the nations.¦layout ªlast_verse.